    description: 'Ilyinets is an impact crater in Ukraine (Vinnytsia Oblast). It is 8.5 kilometres (5.3 mi) in diameter and the age is estimated to be 378 ± 5 million years (Upper Devonian). The crater is not exposed at the surface. The Ilyinets crater is located at the boundary of Ros–Tikych and Dniester–Bug megastructures of the Ukrainian Shield.\n\nAlternative Lore: Ufologists and fringe researchers speculate that Ilyinets crater may hide a deep, covert subterranean facility or D.U.M.B. nested within the impact-compacted bedrock. The natural geological shielding is thought to provide perfect cover for advanced aerospace tests and electromagnetic defense arrays shielded from external satellite scan telemetry.',
