    parentId: 'craters-br',
    name: 'Kamensk Crater',
    description: 'Kamensk crater is an impact crater located 10 to 15 kilometres (6.2 to 9.3 mi) to the north of Kamensk-Shakhtinsky town in Rostov Oblast, Russia. It is 25 km (16 mi) in diameter and the age is estimated to be 49.0 ± 0.2 million years old (Eocene). The crater is not exposed at the surface. It may have formed at the same time as the smaller and nearby Gusev crater.\n\nAlternative Lore: Alternative researchers note that the Kamensk crater site aligns with major planetary grid lines, suggesting it acted as a geological focal point. Dowsers and electromagnetic surveyors report intense magnetic anomalies and local gravitational fluctuations near the rim, leading to claims of a permanent telluric vortex at 48.3500, 40.5000.',
