    parentId: 'craters-br',
    name: 'Nicholson Crater',
    description: 'Nicholson is a meteorite crater in the Northwest Territories, Canada. It is 12.5 kilometres (7.8 mi) in diameter and the age is estimated to be less than 400 million years (Devonian or earlier). The crater is not exposed at the surface.\n\nAlternative Lore: According to alternative history theorists, Nicholson crater represents a ground-zero site of an ancient high-yield thermonuclear blast or particle-beam weapon strike predating recorded history. Proponents point to the extreme presence of shocked quartz and glass-like tektites as evidence of localized artificial vitrification rather than a natural kinetic impact.',
