    description: 'Presqu\'île is a meteorite crater in the territory equivalent to a regional county municipality (TE) of Jamésie in the Nord-du-Québec region of Quebec, Canada, located about 3 kilometres (2 mi) south of the city of Chapais. It is 24 kilometres (15 mi) in diameter and is estimated to be less than 500 million years old (Cambrian period or earlier). The crater is exposed at the surface.\n\nAlternative Lore: This location is cited by catastrophe theorists as a major contributor to a historical global civilization reset. The massive kinetic energy released at Presqu\'île crater is hypothesized to have triggered widespread seismic upheaval, soot clouds, and massive tsunamis, leaving deep scars in local mythology of fire falling from the heavens.',
