    description: 'Puchezh-Katunki is a meteor crater located in the Nizhny Novgorod Oblast of the Volga Federal District, Russia. It is 80 km (50 mi) in diameter. Argon–argon dating has constrained the age of formation to be 195.9 ± 1.0 million years old, placing it within the Sinemurian stage of the Early Jurassic. The crater is not exposed to the surface, but appears as variation in the vegetation. The Earth Impact Database lists a rim-to-rim diameter of 40 kilometres (25 mi).\n\nAlternative Lore: This location is cited by catastrophe theorists as a major contributor to a historical global civilization reset. The massive kinetic energy released at Puchezh-Katunki crater is hypothesized to have triggered widespread seismic upheaval, soot clouds, and massive tsunamis, leaving deep scars in local mythology of fire falling from the heavens.',
