    description: 'Rotmistrivka is an impact crater in Cherkasy Oblast, Ukraine, which is located near the village of Rotmistrivka. The crater is 2.7 kilometres (1.7 mi) in diameter, with an age estimated at 120 ± 10 million years (Lower Cretaceous). It is not exposed to the surface, being buried beneath continental and marine sedimentary deposits. The crater contains a brecciated lens of granite fragments and particles of impact glass, overlain by shales, limestones and granite-derived sandstones of lower Cretaceous age.\n\nAlternative Lore: Some alternative theorists suggest the Rotmistrivka crater event was not a meteoric strike, but the crash site of a massive extraterrestrial vehicle or ancient city-ship. Rumors claim that deep core geological drilling at this location secretly aims to map and retrieve hyper-dense alloy hull components buried beneath the crystalline melt sheets.',
